  "notes": "Reconstructed from Coordinates(blue).pdf by reading the 72 printed label pads off the drawing's own mm ticks (x=(col-0.5)*5.60, y=(row-0.5)*6.05) - the same method reproduces the Gen-1 map exactly from the green drawing, so it was validated before being applied here. Segments 1..36 keep their columns; 37..72 are re-cut and interleaved into the wide strips along the top and bottom edges, so 49/51/55/57 sit on row 1 and 52/54/58/60 on row 20. The label set is exactly mirror-symmetric about the plate centre under (col,row)->(46-col,21-row) - all 18 pairs check - and that symmetry, plus label containment, plus exact tiling of 45x20 pads, leaves one reading. Segment counts per strip left to right are 4,6,6,4,2,6,6,4,6,6,2,4,6,6,4: themselves mirror-symmetric, summing to 72, covering 900 pads. CONSEQUENCE: segments 9-16 and 21-28 are 6.776 cm2 here against 8.470 cm2 on Gen 1, because those strips each gave two pad rows to a new edge segment. Never carry an area across generations. Residual uncertainty: the exact pad-row boundary inside strips carrying more than four segments is constrained by the labels to within one pad row. Verify once against the KiCad board file to remove it.",
